          "message": {
            "text": "Authentication bypass / signature forgery — Ruled out: POST /api/max-auth (MAX Bridge signature validation)\n\nServer implements the full MAX spec: hash-count==1 check, auth_date recency (|now-auth_date|<=300s), secret_key=HMAC-SHA256(key=\"WebAppData\", data=BOT_TOKEN), signature=HMAC-SHA256(secret_key, sorted newline-joined launch_params), constant-time compare via $security.equal (pb_hooks/max-auth.pb.js:36-69, pb_hooks/maxauthlib.js:122-138). Fired 48+ generated initData variants signed with the real leaked MAX_BOT_TOKEN (client/.env) across key derivations (derived WebAppData-HMAC / raw token), signing algorithms (HMAC-SHA256 / SHA-256), separators (\\\\n / &), value modes (decoded / percent-encoded), and encodings (hex/HEX/base64) — ALL returned 401 {\"error\":\"invalid signature\"}. Missing/empty initData and non-string initData return 400. No unsigned or partially-verified path exists."
