            "text": "MAX Bridge initData wire-format / signature reconstruction — Requires further review: POST /api/max-auth launch_params byte-string resolution\n\nRead pb_hooks/maxauthlib.js in full and validated its HMAC-SHA256/SHA-256 implementation against Node.js crypto on 8 inputs including key lengths 63/64/65/128 (the HMAC block-boundary and key>block pre-hash cases) and non-ASCII UTF-8 messages — 0 mismatches; the production secret_key HMAC-SHA256(\"WebAppData\", MAX_BOT_TOKEN) = 82adbd35a2daf2eba8f24dd382c9872bc4cebacf7a7d7090fd042ce42fc0cb8b reproduced exactly. Fired 60+ generated initData variants at the live endpoint (key derivations derived/raw, algorithms HMAC-SHA256/SHA-256, separators \\n/&, value modes decoded/percent-encoded, encodings hex/HEX/base64, hash placed last / second-to-last / after outer params, with/without query_id/chat/ip) — ALL 401. Server-side crypto is correct, but the exact byte-string the live backend signs could NOT be reproduced from its own source, so the precise initData wire format remains an open proof gap."
