            "text": "Broken function-level authorization on custom hook routes — Ruled out: Custom /api/* PocketBase hook routes (moderator-gated set)\n\nTested as a plain `user` token against every custom route. All return a role check before any side effect: /api/bot-notify-training-status|edit|cancelled|restored|create -> 403; /api/users-claim-candidates|claim-max|unclaim-max -> 403; /api/users-create-manual -> 403; /api/admin-backup -> 403; /api/admin-dispatch-now -> 403; /api/users-delete -> 403; /api/system-templates -> 403; /api/internal/backup-notify -> 403. Source confirms the `auth.getString('role') !== 'moderator'` gate at each routerAdd site. Only /api/bot-notify-training lacked it (reported separately)."
