        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/authorization-bypass-via-state-transition-branch",
          "ruleIndex": 22,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Authorization bypass via state-transition branch — Requires further review: PATCH trainings — is_cancelled false->true / true->false (cancel/restore transition bypass)\n\nClosed by correlating the peer's result with mine rather than leaving it open. The peer concluded the cancel/restore branches (trainingslib.js:437-483) are \"unreachable for a non-privileged user\" because is_cancelled is not in TRAINING_USER_EDITABLE and assertTrainingUpdateAllowed rejects it. My testing confirms the rejection is real but shows WHY: the wrapper at trainingslib.js:395 means assertTrainingUpdateAllowed is the only thing that stops it, and it rejects on the field name rather than on the transition. Live differential on qs808160ey9ib5q with the user token: {\"is_cancelled\":true,\"attended_users\":[self]} -> 403 naming is_cancelled; {\"booked_users\":[self]} -> 200 vs {\"booked_users\":[self,other]} -> 403 \"Можно записать только себя\". So the guard at 395-413 does execute, and it does not evaluate attended_users inside a cancel transition; the two layers share one client-controlled precondition. The isCancelTransition branch itself I also could not land: of 25 consecutive attempts at {\"is_cancelled\":true,\"booked_users\":[]} every reply was 403 or 502, never 200, while no-change bodies returned 200 immediately. Net: this is a genuine defect (removable authorization control + a traced write to users.attendance_count at line 491), correctly downgraded to Low because the counter increment was never observed and the only reachable training has already ended (if (!ended) at line 473 skips it). Full detail, the exact differential, the regression commit and the proposed patch are on the shared note titled \"FINDING (primary): trainingslib.js:395 guard gated on client-supplied is_cancelled\". Root-cause-idor-trainingslib395 is an OPEN PROOF GAP for the end-to-end write only."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "PATCH trainings — is_cancelled false->true / true->false (cancel/restore transition bypass)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
