          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stored XSS into other users' in-app notifications — Ruled out: notifications collection + /api/notify-comment-reply (comment_replies_lib.js)\n\nServer-side hook (pb_hooks/comment_replies_lib.js) writes an in-app `notifications` record with title=actor full_name, body=parent comment text (stripHtmlToPlain strips tags), badge_text=reply text, meta with raw actor.full_name/avatar_url. User-controlled input DOES reach these fields, but: (a) a normal user cannot change full_name (PATCH full_name -> 403 \"Изменение поля full_name недоступно\" via users_access_guard_lib.js SELF_EDITABLE_ALWAYS allow-list, which also blocks can_comment/is_visible/max_id/rating_points), so the name vector is closed; (b) comment text is HTML-stripped before storage; (c) POST self-notification succeeded (200, id k4p4l299ke15ey7) but only self-addressed, while recipient=OTHER was rejected (400 \"Failed to create record\", createRule @request.auth.id != \"\" && (recipient = @request.auth.id || role = moderator)); read list is self-scoped (totalItems: 2, all mine). The only exposure is self-XSS requiring the victim to write their own comment. Probe record deleted (204)."
