            "text": "Weak passwords / auth endpoint misconfiguration / account enumeration — No issue identified: users auth collection endpoints (auth-with-password / otp / oauth2 / reset / impersonate)\n\nProbed every auth endpoint. auth-with-password exists and is enabled (returns 400 \"Failed to authenticate.\" for any wrong password, incl. the correct email of the real account); OTP returns 403 \"not configured to allow OTP authentication\"; OAuth2 returns 403 \"not configured to allow OAuth2 authentication\"; confirm-password-reset validates the token (400 validation_invalid_token); /users/impersonate 404; /_superusers/auth-with-password exists (separate superuser collection). No endpoint leaked account existence (request-password-reset uniform 204/timing; auth-with-password uniform 400). ~2 wrong-password attempts total, well under budget; no brute force performed."
