        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/server-side-template-injection-via-interpolate-resolve",
          "ruleIndex": 30,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Server-side template injection via interpolate()/resolve() — Ruled out: pb_hooks/templatelib.js interpolate()/resolve()\n\nRan templatelib.js under Node with PocketBase globals stubbed. `interpolate(text,vars)` splits on `{{k}}` for each key of `vars` and joins — a single pass with no re-scan. Injecting `{{time}}`/`{{name}}`/`{{count}}` via a user-controlled `full_name` (the `actor` var) survives verbatim into the output and is never expanded. `${7*7}`, `%s` and HTML also pass through unmodified. resolve() call sites all pass compile-time literal keys (grep of bot_notifications.pb.js, comment_replies_lib.js, mention_notifications_lib.js, notification libs). Confirms the two-pass template expansion hypothesis is impossible; the residual concern is only stored markup in a MAX markdown message or a React-rendered card."
