          "ruleIndex": 31,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stored XSS via injected markup in notification title/body — Ruled out: client/src/features/notifications/NotificationCard.jsx + postRichText.js toDisplayHtml\n\nClient render path traced: NotificationCard.jsx renders notification.title/body through PostContentHtml -> toDisplayHtml() in client/src/features/feed/postRichText.js, a DOMParser-based allow-list sanitizer (tags B/STRONG/I/EM/U/A/BR/DIV/P/SPAN/IMG; per-tag attribute allow-list; href must match ^https?:// or mailto:; IMG src must match ^https?://|/|data:image/; all attribute values escapeHtml'd). A plain-string actor name such as `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>` fails looksLikeRichHtml() and is fully escapeHtml'd, so no tag survives. The comment/mention path stores only the actor name as a literal string, not attacker HTML. No bypass found."
