        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/api3-broken-object-property-level-authorization-over-exposure",
          "ruleIndex": 32,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "API3 Broken object property level authorization (over-exposure) — Requires further review: GET /api/collections/users/records (list + view)\n\nWith a plain `user` token, GET /api/collections/users/records (list) and /records/{otherId} (view) return every other member's private fields: email (or `null` when the member hid it), max_id, birth_date, membership_start_date/end_date/type, available_sessions, used_sessions, unpaid_sessions, rating_points, attendance_count, ban_reason, membership_frozen, avatar_url. The collection rule is `@request.auth.id != \"\"` for both list and view, so this applies to every member. Confirmed by reading both the own and a moderator's record. This is a pre-existing over-exposure of member PII/financial data in the schema's design, not something introduced by the tested hook code, and it is likely intended for the app's member directory (client/src/services/users.js requests a narrower `fields` set: id,collectionId,collectionName,full_name,avatar,avatar_url), which suggests the unrestricted read is not needed by the SPA."
          },
