        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/self-service-privilege-escalation-server-authoritative-value-forgery-rating-attendance-membership",
          "ruleIndex": 33,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Self-service privilege escalation / server-authoritative value forgery (rating, attendance, membership) — Ruled out: users collection self-update + client-side rating_points increment\n\nTested the client-side `applyTournamentPostSideEffects` path (client/src/services/tournamentPosts.js:244-252) which calls `pb.collection('users').update(userId, {'rating_points+': points})` directly from the browser, duplicating the server hook. A plain user cannot reach it: POST /api/collections/tournament_posts/records returns 400 \"Failed to create record\" (createRule is `@request.auth.role = \"moderator\"`), so the code never runs for non-moderators. Independently, the users field-level ACL in pb_hooks/users_access_guard_lib.js rejects rating_points/attendance_count/available_sessions/used_sessions/unpaid_sessions/wins/losses/is_banned/can_comment/is_visible/role/max_id changes by a non-privileged caller with 403 'Изменение поля \"<f>\" недоступно.' — verified live for rating_points (own record -> 403) and attendance_count (own record -> 403), and PATCH of another user's record returns 404 (rule `id = @request.auth.id`)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "users collection self-update + client-side rating_points increment"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Self-service privilege escalation / server-authoritative value forgery (rating, attendance, membership)",
              "surface": "users collection self-update + client-side rating_points increment",
              "recorded_by": "SSTI/RCE & Injection Hunter",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/json-prototype-pollution-in-participants-handling-achievement-progress-forgery",
          "ruleIndex": 34,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "JSON/prototype pollution in participants handling; achievement progress forgery — Ruled out: achievementslib.parseParticipants + countUserTournamentPlacesFromPosts\n\nRead achievementslib.js parseParticipants and exercised it under Node with hostile inputs: `__proto__`/`constructor.prototype` payloads, string/number/object instead of array, nested arrays, string and negative and 1e308 place values, null elements, object-typed userId. parseParticipants returns [] for every non-array shape, `Object.prototype` remains unpolluted, and countUserTournamentPlacesFromPosts counts only the FIRST matching entry per post (so duplicate entries cannot inflate counts). Combined with `achievements`/`achievement_levels`/`tournament_posts` all being moderator-write, and rating_points being denied by the field ACL, no forgery path exists from a member account."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "achievementslib.parseParticipants + countUserTournamentPlacesFromPosts"
                }
              ]
            }
