              "risk_area": "SSRF / path traversal / CRLF header injection",
              "surface": "/api/yadisk-preview and /api/yadisk-content (yadisklib.js)",
              "recorded_by": "SSTI/RCE & Injection Hunter",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/pocketbase-filter-injection-via-string-concatenation",
          "ruleIndex": 36,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "PocketBase filter injection via string concatenation — Ruled out: pb_hooks filter construction (all findRecordsByFilter call sites)\n\nSwept every `findRecordsByFilter`/`findFirstRecordByFilter` call site in pb_hooks. All filter strings are built from server-derived values only: templatelib uses compile-time literal keys ('key = \"' + d.key + '\"'), achievementslib uses numeric sort_order and moderator-written achievement ids, statslib dates pass a strict /^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/ check in parsePeriod before use, notificationslib/mention_notifications_lib/comment_replies_lib interpolate record-derived recipient/author ids, and claimlib binds the one user-supplied value through the `{:exclude}` parameter form. No attacker-controlled string is concatenated into a PocketBase filter, so filter breakout (quote/`||`/`&&`/`@request.auth`) is not reachable."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
