        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/bfla-privilege-escalation-via-granting-achievement-levels",
          "ruleIndex": 38,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "BFLA / privilege escalation via granting achievement levels — Ruled out: POST|PATCH|DELETE /api/collections/achievements, /api/collections/achievement_levels\n\nschema.json createRule/updateRule/deleteRule = `@request.auth.role = \"moderator\"` for both collections. Live with a role=user token: POST /api/collections/achievements/records -> 400 \"Failed to create record.\"; PATCH/DELETE on an existing achievement id -> 404; same for achievement_levels. No 2xx response was ever returned. Moderator-only writes are therefore enforced at the collection rule, before any hook."
