        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/bfla-on-custom-pb-hooks-routeradd-endpoints-forged-achievement-state",
          "ruleIndex": 39,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "BFLA on custom pb_hooks routerAdd endpoints; forged achievement state — No issue identified: Custom pb_hooks routes /api/stats/*, /api/admin-*, /api/bot-notify-*, /api/content-view\n\nEnumerated all routerAdd endpoints in pb_hooks (stats.pb.js, admin_scheduler.pb.js, backup.pb.js, bot_notifications.pb.js, user*_claim/manual/delete.pb.js, yadisk.pb.js, video_poster.pb.js, max-auth.pb.js, shop_audit.pb.js, comment_replies.pb.js, membership_lifecycle.pb.js). Every /api/stats/* route calls stats.requireModerator(c) first (stats.pb.js:28,44,60,86,102,118,138,158,172); /api/admin-dispatch-now, /api/admin-backup and the /api/bot-notify-* routes each check `auth.getString('role') !== 'moderator'`. /api/content-view and /api/max-auth are intentionally auth-only. No unauthenticated or user-reachable moderator function found. No server-side persistence of achievement state exists at all (getAchievementsNow/getAchievementGrants are read-only aggregations)."
          },
