        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/rating-placement-forgery-via-tournament-posts-participants",
          "ruleIndex": 42,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Rating/placement forgery via tournament_posts.participants — Ruled out: POST|PATCH /api/collections/tournament_posts/records (+ postslib.applyTournamentRating)\n\ntournament_posts create/update/delete rules are all `@request.auth.role = \"moderator\"` in schema.json; the rating award path pb_hooks/postslib.js:8-37 (applyTournamentRating, $app.save on users.rating_points) is only invoked from moderator-gated saves. Live with a role=user token: POST /api/collections/tournament_posts/records -> 403, PATCH -> 403. The participants JSON (with the attacker-relevant userId/place/points fields) is therefore not writable by a plain user, so rating_points cannot be forged through this route and the podium/first-place achievement inputs (achievementslib.js:32-63, client/src/services/achievements.js:117-132) are moderator-controlled. Note as a design observation (not a finding): client/src/services/tournamentPosts.js:250 does a client-side `pb.collection('users').update(participant.userId, {'rating_points+': points})` which would be rejected by the users field allow-list for the same reason."
          },
