        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/unauthorized-modification-of-training-metadata-and-other-members-bookings",
          "ruleIndex": 43,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthorized modification of training metadata and other members' bookings — Ruled out: PATCH /api/collections/trainings/records/{id} — metadata fields and booked_users=[other]\n\nLive with a role=user token on training qs808160ey9ib5q, all stable across repeats (independent of the proxy's intermittent 502s): {\"date\":...} -> 403 'date'; {\"location\":\"HACKTEST\"} -> 403 'location'; {\"is_deleted\":true} -> 403 'is_deleted'; {\"is_cancelled\":false,\"attended_users\":[self]} -> 403 'attended_users'; {\"booked_users\":[other-id]} -> 403 'Можно записать только себя'. These are the enforcement paths that DO work, and they pin down the trigger conditions referenced in the primary finding: TRAINING_USER_EDITABLE (trainingslib.js:304-310) plus TRAINING_COMPARE_FIELDS (312-318) plus assertTrainingUpdateAllowed (359-372) correctly reject every metadata/booking field except the five booking arrays, and the booked_users self-only check fires on newlyAdded !== []."
          },
          "locations": [
