        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/end-to-end-persistence-of-forged-attendance-count-achievement-grant",
          "ruleIndex": 44,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "End-to-end persistence of forged attendance_count / achievement grant — Requires further review: trainings attended_users → users.attendance_count → achievement grant (end-to-end write)\n\nCOULD NOT CLOSE. The reachable path is source-traced end to end: applyBookingSideEffects restore branch (trainingslib.js:472-494) calls adjustAttendanceCountTx(txApp, restoreAttended[i], +1) (line 493) for every id in record.attended_users with the guard at line 395 skipped, and adjustAttendanceCountTx (trainingslib.js:266-276) writes users.attendance_count unconditionally; maybeGrantAchievementLevels (achievementslib.js:124-176) then logs 'profile.achievement.grant' off that counter. What is MISSING is the captured 2xx: I never observed the request that actually persisted the increment. Two blockers, both environmental rather than code: (1) the cancel half of the cycle requires is_cancelled to flip together with a booked_users change, and in a 29-reply sweep of new PWAs every reply to that specific root type was 403/400 ('Q68J8Bqz66Z7vGnzZ6xP'), 502 or 422 ('k9X25Z7Sg22y3G19YK4wQ'), never 200; (2) the periodic handler E updates keep reprinting root 1siE8cDnVAq1yXgzvv4Po7 state only, and the token in /workspace/.tennis-recon/token.txt rotates on every auth-refresh, so the accepted write and its cleanup could not be sequenced atomically. Because the record is one-shot per training (the transition cannot be repeated once is_cancelled is true) I did not want to burn the last live record without a captured response. Next step is a single instrumented request log on the cancel+restore pair, or a fresh test training created by a moderator account."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "trainings attended_users → users.attendance_count → achievement grant (end-to-end write)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "needs_follow_up",
              "risk_area": "End-to-end persistence of forged attendance_count / achievement grant",
              "surface": "trainings attended_users → users.attendance_count → achievement grant (end-to-end write)",
              "recorded_by": "Achievements & Score Forgery Hunter",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/stored-xss-via-posts-content-comments-text-tournament-gallery-comments-domparser-sanitized-pipeline",
          "ruleIndex": 45,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stored XSS via posts.content / comments.text / tournament & gallery comments (DOMParser-sanitized pipeline) — Ruled out: client/src/features/feed/postRichText.js sanitizePostHtml/serializeSanitized + PostContentHtml render chain\n\nEnumerated every client HTML sink: only `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` is `PostContentHtml.jsx:108,120` fed by `toDisplayHtml()` -> `sanitizePostHtml()` (DOMParser + ALLOWED_TAGS/ALLOWED_ATTRS allowlist) -> `linkifyPlainUrls()`. Also `PostRichTextField.jsx:579 el.innerHTML = toDisplayHtml(next)` (same sanitizer). No eval/new Function/document.write/srcdoc in client/src. Tested live and in a jsdom replica: plain-text `<img src=x onerror=...>` -> HTML-escaped; `<b <img ...>>` -> `<b></b>`; `<span contenteditable=\"true\">` -> bare text (all attributes dropped by the SPAN/DIV/P branch at postRichText.js:327-336); mention spans always re-emitted with contenteditable=\"false\" by serializeMentionEl (postMentions.js:599-621). `escapeHtml` omits `'` but every serialized attribute is double-quoted (verified with jsdom that a raw `<`/`>`/backtick inside a quoted attribute stays inert), so no breakout."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "client/src/features/feed/postRichText.js sanitizePostHtml/serializeSanitized + PostContentHtml render chain"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Stored XSS via posts.content / comments.text / tournament & gallery comments (DOMParser-sanitized pipeline)",
              "surface": "client/src/features/feed/postRichText.js sanitizePostHtml/serializeSanitized + PostContentHtml render chain",
              "recorded_by": "Frontend XSS & Client-Trust Hunter",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/dom-based-xss-via-url-hash-query-parameters-and-postmessage",
          "ruleIndex": 46,
          "kind": "notApplicable",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "DOM-based XSS via URL/hash/query parameters and postMessage — Not applicable: client/src (location.*, postMessage, service worker registration, URL parsing)\n\nGrepped client/src for location.hash/searchParams/addEventListener('message'/document.referrer/srcdoc. Only two hits, both non-attacker-controlled: `ForceUpdateOverlay.jsx` builds a URL with `searchParams.set('_v', Date.now())` for a cache-busting reload, and `main.jsx` reads `window.location.origin` to register the service worker. No postMessage listener, no URL/hash-to-sink flow, no `window.name`/opener usage. DOM-XSS surface not present."
          },
