        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/client-side-trust-of-role-for-admin-ui-forgeable-localstorage-authstore-moderation-gating",
          "ruleIndex": 48,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Client-side trust of role for admin UI (forgeable localStorage authStore) / moderation gating — Ruled out: client/src/services/auth.js isModerator + App.jsx admin tab + /api/users-create-manual\n\n`isModerator()` (client/src/services/auth.js:181) reads `pb.authStore.model` from localStorage and gates App.jsx:312/316/485/654-655 (admin tab, admin \"+\" and nav items) plus useRegisterAddAction call sites (RatingPage, CompetitionsPage, TrainingsPage, ShopPage). Verified live that every privileged endpoint behind that UI enforces the role server-side: PATCH users fields `rating_points`/`membership_comment`/`can_comment`/`is_visible`/`email`/`max_id` -> 403, `POST /api/users-create-manual` -> 403, foreign comment PATCH -> 404. Forging `role=moderator` in localStorage therefore reveals the admin UI but yields no privileged server response: UI-only gate, no capability escalation. Reported only as context, not as a standalone finding."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "client/src/services/auth.js isModerator + App.jsx admin tab + /api/users-create-manual"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Client-side trust of role for admin UI (forgeable localStorage authStore) / moderation gating",
              "surface": "client/src/services/auth.js isModerator + App.jsx admin tab + /api/users-create-manual",
              "recorded_by": "Frontend XSS & Client-Trust Hunter",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/client-side-trust-of-ban-block-state-via-sessionstorage",
          "ruleIndex": 49,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Client-side trust of ban / block state via sessionStorage — Ruled out: client/src/services/auth.js ban info storage + BlockedPage gate\n\n`banInfo` is persisted in `sessionStorage['tennis_ban_info']` (auth.js:37,51-71) and consumed by `getInitialUser()`/`BlockedPage.jsx`; `isUserBanned()` prefers the server-side `user.is_banned` from the token/record. Tampering with sessionStorage can only hide the local blocked screen for the attacker's own browser; it does not alter server-side `is_banned`, and the users access guard (pb_hooks/users_access_guard_lib.js) rejects all non-whitelisted field updates, so a banned user cannot clear their own flag. Client-only cosmetic bypass, no security consequence on its own."
          },
          "locations": [
