        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/forged-mention-notifications-user-regex-server-regex-differential-in-extractusermentionids",
          "ruleIndex": 50,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Forged mention notifications: user-regex/server-regex differential in extractUserMentionIds — Requires further review: pb_hooks/mention_notifications_lib.js extractUserMentionIds + comments.text / posts.content\n\nTraced the mention pipeline: server-side `extractUserMentionIds` in pb_hooks/mention_notifications_lib.js scans `<span ...>` tags in comments.text/posts.content and regex-extracts the first `data-user-id` per tag, then creates a notification for each id (mention_notifications.pb.js fires on create/update). Modelled it in node against sanitized output: a user-controlled floating `data-user-id=\"X\"` before the real attributes is preserved verbatim by the client sanitizer (which re-emits the FIRST `data-user-id` it finds) and parsed by the server regex, so a member could point a mention chip at a spoofed user id and trigger a notification to an arbitrary real user with forged mention copy. The impact is the same class of forged-notification spoofing already filed as vuln-0007 for the notifications collection, and the written evidence is a source+regex model rather than a live end-to-end replay (I did not fire it at a real user's inbox). Recording the gap rather than claiming it."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "pb_hooks/mention_notifications_lib.js extractUserMentionIds + comments.text / posts.content"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "needs_follow_up",
              "risk_area": "Forged mention notifications: user-regex/server-regex differential in extractUserMentionIds",
              "surface": "pb_hooks/mention_notifications_lib.js extractUserMentionIds + comments.text / posts.content",
              "recorded_by": "Frontend XSS & Client-Trust Hunter",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/field-parsing-type-coercion-bypass-in-the-moderator-only-manual-user-creation-endpoint",
          "ruleIndex": 51,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Field parsing / type-coercion bypass in the moderator-only manual user creation endpoint — Requires further review: POST /api/users-create-manual (pb_hooks/users_manual.pb.js, manualuserlib.js)\n\nImplements manual player creation with a server-side `auth.getString('role') !== 'moderator'` gate (verified live: 403 for a plain user). Field parsing uses `asString()` which unwraps single-element arrays, and `rating_points` is coerced with `Number(...) || 0`. A potential goja type-coercion differential in the array/object branches could not be exercised because no moderator token was available for this engagement; the gate itself is present and correct on the paths tested."
