            "text": "Confidentiality of other users' comments (cross-user read) — No issue identified: GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/collections/comments/records\n\nComments are readable across users for any authenticated account (listRule `@request.auth.id != \"\"`), which allows enumerating other members' comment ids and content. Storing/updating remains ownership-scoped (PATCH and DELETE on a foreign comment both returned 404), and the read scope was explicitly treated as intended product behaviour rather than a finding. Noted so a later agent does not re-report cross-user comment reads as a confidentiality bug."
