        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/broken-function-level-authorization-on-broadcast-template-mutation-routes",
          "ruleIndex": 57,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Broken function-level authorization on broadcast / template-mutation routes — Ruled out: /api/bot-notify-training-status, -edit, -create, -cancelled, -restored; /api/max-bot-webhook; /api/bot-notify-membership-frozen; /api/notify-membership-topup; /api/system-templates; /api/system-templates-update\n\nAnonymous -> 401, role=user -> 403 for bot-notify-training-status, -edit, -create, -cancelled, -restored, even with realistic bodies containing a nonexistent trainingId and valid `changes` arrays — so the role check precedes all record lookup and every broadcastToAllUsers path. /api/max-bot-webhook -> 403 for both anonymous and authenticated callers unless the X-Max-Bot-Api-Secret header matches MAX_BOT_WEBHOOK_SECRET (bot_notifications.pb.js:397-406); tested with no header, \"test\", and \"0\". /api/bot-notify-membership-frozen and /api/notify-membership-topup -> 403 for both anonymous and user (membership_lifecycle.pb.js:25-27 / 42-45). /api/system-templates -> 403 anon and user; /api/system-templates-update -> 403 for both even with a valid-shaped `{\"id\":\"zqath3x\",\"title\":\"t\"}` body, so the gate precedes the record lookup."
          },
          "locations": [
