        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/broken-function-level-authorization-via-route-shadowing-verb-drift",
          "ruleIndex": 59,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Broken function-level authorization via route shadowing / verb drift — Ruled out: Route-shape bypasses on moderator-only custom routes (method override, trailing slash, case, encoded slash, doubled slash)\n\nTested method overrides, trailing slashes and case variants against a moderator-only route with the user token: X-HTTP-Method-Override: GET -> 404, trailing slash -> 404, GET /API/System-Templates -> 200 but body is the React SPA index.html (nginx static fallback, not the API handler — confirmed by the `<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"ru\">` body). Every other verb/path-shape combination (PUT/PATCH/DELETE/POST on `/api/stats/growth`, `/api/stats/growth/`, `/api/Stats/Growth`, `/api/stats/growth%2f`, `/api/users-claim-candidates/`) returned PocketBase 404 \"File not found\"/\"resource wasn't found\", never a 200 from the guarded handler. `/api/stats//growth` returned 301 to the canonical path, which then enforces 403."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
