        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/broken-function-level-authorization-via-jwt-claim-trust-role-collectionid-claims",
          "ruleIndex": 60,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Broken function-level authorization via JWT claim trust (role / collectionId claims) — Ruled out: Custom-route moderator gate vs tampered JWT claims (collectionId confusion, injected role claim)\n\nTen forged-token variants re-signed with the original (invalid) signature were rejected 401: `collectionId:\"\"`, `collectionId` swapped to another collection id, `collectionId` omitted entirely, and an added `\"role\":\"moderator\"` claim. Decisive result: the forged token whose payload carries `role:\"moderator\"` still gets `401 Unauthorized` from `/api/stats/growth` and `/api/stats/achievements`, whereas the genuine token gets `403 Forbidden` — proving the server resolves `auth.getString('role')` from the users record and ignores any role claim carried in the JWT. The same forged token also fails record-scoped reads (404), so no privilege came from the tampered claims."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Custom-route moderator gate vs tampered JWT claims (collectionId confusion, injected role claim)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Broken function-level authorization via JWT claim trust (role / collectionId claims)",
              "surface": "Custom-route moderator gate vs tampered JWT claims (collectionId confusion, injected role claim)",
              "recorded_by": "Admin Endpoint BFLA Hunter",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/ssrf-path-traversal-arbitrary-outbound-fetch",
          "ruleIndex": 61,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "SSRF / path traversal / arbitrary outbound fetch — Ruled out: /api/yadisk-preview, /api/yadisk-content (url + path parameters)\n\nAnonymous -> 401 for /api/yadisk-preview and /api/yadisk-content. With the user token, every non-Yandex destination was rejected client-side by the YADISK_URL_RE allowlist (yadisklib.js:7) before any outbound request: `http://127.0.0.1:8090/api/health`, `http://localhost/`, `http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/`, `https://evil.example/d/x`, `file:///etc/passwd` all returned `400 {\"error\":\"Некорректная ссылка Яндекс.Диска\"}`. The suffix-confusion candidate `https://disk.yandex.ru.evil.example/d/x` was also rejected 400 (the regex anchors the host with no `/` allowed before `/d/`). Outbound fetches are built from the constant cloud-api.yandex.net host with the user URL only as an encoded `public_key` query parameter. `path` traversal (`../../../../etc/passwd`, `/../../etc/passwd`, `disk:/../../etc/passwd`) returned 404 from the Yandex metadata API, not a local file."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/api/yadisk-preview, /api/yadisk-content (url + path parameters)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "SSRF / path traversal / arbitrary outbound fetch",
              "surface": "/api/yadisk-preview, /api/yadisk-content (url + path parameters)",
              "recorded_by": "Admin Endpoint BFLA Hunter",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/broken-function-level-authorization-unbounded-resource-consumption-on-the-custom-content-view-writer",
          "ruleIndex": 62,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Broken function-level authorization / unbounded resource consumption on the custom content-view writer — No issue identified: POST /api/content-view (custom route) and direct POST /api/collections/content_views/records\n\nAnonymous -> 401. With the user token, `{\"object_type\":\"x\",\"object_id\":\"y\"}` -> 400 `object_type must be post or tournament_post` and a valid-shaped `{\"object_type\":\"post\",\"object_id\":\"zqath3probe\",\"source\":\"viewport\"}` -> 200 `{\"id\":\"pk094mpvi67cd8b\",\"ok\":true}`. The only write is one content_views row with `user` forced to the caller's own id (statslib.js createContentView sets `record.set('user', userId)` from auth), so this is a self-scoped analytics row, not a privileged action. No update/delete and no cross-user write. The row created during testing carries the `zqath3probe` marker object_id; content_views has no delete rule so it cannot be removed via the API."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "POST /api/content-view (custom route) and direct POST /api/collections/content_views/records"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
