            "text": "Broken function-level authorization / audit-log integrity — No issue identified: POST /api/audit-buy-click\n\nAnonymous -> 401; with the user token `{\"productIds\":[\"fwlj07b87160284\"]}` -> 200 `{\"ok\":true}`. The handler writes one audit_events row whose `subject` is derived server-side from `audit.actorInfo(auth)` with `source:'self'` (shop_audit.pb.js:148-190), so a user can only create an audit record attributed to themselves. Impact confirmed bounded: the caller cannot read it back — `GET /api/collections/audit_events/records` with the same user token returns 200 with `{\"items\":[],\"totalItems\":0}` because the rule is `@request.auth.role = \"moderator\"`. No privileged action, no cross-user effect, no data disclosure."
